# VisionAI General Rules

- Use clean, modular, human-readable code.
- Always check existing implementation before writing new utilities.
- Keep functions single-purpose and under 50 lines where practical.
- Never hardcode configuration parameters; pull them from `app/config.py` or `.env`.
- Write meaningful commit messages following Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `test:`).
- Read `docs/PRD.md` and `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` before making architectural updates.
